From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:42:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 203/204] security/tpm: Keep the pre-RAM TPM log inside its
 region

The TPM 1.2 and TPM 2.0 formats of the pre-RAM log set its limit to
MAX_TPM_LOG_ENTRIES (50), the one of the log in cbmem, while the
TPM_LOG region is 2 KiB on x86 (car.ld), room for 16 to 24 entries
depending on the format and TPM_MEASURED_BOOT_SHA1_BANK. The entries
after those go into the region after it, the pre-RAM console in car.ld,
and recover_tpm_log() then refuses to copy a log of more than
MAX_PRERAM_TPM_LOG_ENTRIES (15) at all.

Set the limit of the pre-RAM log to the entries that fit in the region,
and no more than MAX_PRERAM_TPM_LOG_ENTRIES, as the coreboot format
does: a further measurement is left out of the log ("log table is
full"; before the TPM starts, out of the PCRs too, as they are replayed
from the log), and the entries before it reach cbmem.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c |  9 ++++++++-
 src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm2.c | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c b/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c
index dc1f64eab6..e807b2547a 100644
--- a/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c
+++ b/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c
@@ -138,7 +138,14 @@ void tpm1_preram_log_clear(void)
 	 * is not initialized.
 	 */
 	struct tpm_1_log_table *tclt = (struct tpm_1_log_table *)_tpm_log;
-	tclt->vendor.max_entries = htole16(MAX_TPM_LOG_ENTRIES);
+	/*
+	 * Only the entries that fit in the TPM_LOG region: past it is the
+	 * pre-RAM console (car.ld). No more than the pre-RAM log may hold
+	 * when it is copied into cbmem (recover_tpm_log()).
+	 */
+	size_t fit = REGION_SIZE(tpm_log) > sizeof(*tclt) ?
+		(REGION_SIZE(tpm_log) - sizeof(*tclt)) / sizeof(tclt->entries[0]) : 0;
+	tclt->vendor.max_entries = htole16(MIN(fit, MAX_PRERAM_TPM_LOG_ENTRIES));
 	tclt->vendor.num_entries = htole16(0);
 }
 
diff --git a/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm2.c b/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm2.c
index 479c718313..00c227be9e 100644
--- a/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm2.c
+++ b/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm2.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <symbols.h>
 #include <cbmem.h>
+#include <commonlib/bsd/helpers.h>
 #include <vb2_sha.h>
 
 static uint16_t tpmalg_from_vb2_hash(enum vb2_hash_algorithm hash_type)
@@ -247,7 +248,14 @@ void tpm2_preram_log_clear(void)
 	 * is not initialized.
 	 */
 	struct tpm_2_log_table *tclt = (struct tpm_2_log_table *)_tpm_log;
-	tclt->vendor.max_entries = htole16(MAX_TPM_LOG_ENTRIES);
+	/*
+	 * Only the entries that fit in the TPM_LOG region: past it is the
+	 * pre-RAM console (car.ld). No more than the pre-RAM log may hold
+	 * when it is copied into cbmem (recover_tpm_log()).
+	 */
+	size_t fit = REGION_SIZE(tpm_log) > sizeof(*tclt) ?
+		(REGION_SIZE(tpm_log) - sizeof(*tclt)) / sizeof(tclt->entries[0]) : 0;
+	tclt->vendor.max_entries = htole16(MIN(fit, MAX_PRERAM_TPM_LOG_ENTRIES));
 	tclt->vendor.num_entries = htole16(0);
 }
 
